{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398785-10th-sphere-and-what-those-new-spheres-mean","id":1398785,"title":"10th Sphere and What those New Spheres Mean","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-25T08:02:24-07:00","id":1398785,"title":"10th Sphere and What those New Spheres Mean","content":"The Hermetics and the Ahl-i-Batin all convinced the other Traditions to adopt a Nine Sphere system for at least talking about things. Seems a good way to bring about order, or ... a good way to bring a base Paradigm that they all share, just without telling them. The idea of the sphere system is based on Kaballah (I'm going to ignore the Qlippoth here, you can fill that into your theory later if you like.) Kaballah is a Hebrew word, and what does that word mean 'Correspondence', and there is no 10th Sphere in Kaballah 10 is 1 is 0. Emanation flows through the first Sphere, through the other, and out the final Sphere. In addition, most Spheres exist in duality, but some do not.<br /> <br /> Check out the ordering Ahl-I-Batin gives to the Kaballah, check out Order of Hermes revised and how they /Renamed/ the Sphere in Latin, supposedly to make them more correct, but Turning the 'Sphere of Spirits' into the 'Sphere of Ghosts' ? Giving Prime and Forces practically the same name and dividing them? And if Prime is the one, how can you rename the one. Not like the Hermetics thing that words of power ....<br /> <br /> Now look at the overlaps between Correspondence-Data-Spirit-Dimensional Science, and how Primal Utility seems to suggest something new taking the place of Prime, basically Base matter having been turned to gold.<br /> <br /> Look at the Symbols for all the Spheres, the ones all the Traditions use. Notice two are the same for 'amalgam (process of)' and 'amalgamation (thing')<br /> <br /> Look at the Order of Hermes Revised Foci. Why would you use a symbol of Mars to evoke Mercury? How could you use either 4 or 5 for Matter? Just read all the weird things in the section, and it makes sense why Brucato didn't want to fully explain their Paradigm there.<br /> <br /> Also explains why every book hints at a weirdness with Shard and Shade realms.<br /> <br /> And the Virtual Adepts are now the Mercurial Elite? In charge of Correspondence/Data? Mercury the Trickster having hidden himself and defeated the Nephandi at their own game.<br /> <br /> Too bad about all those Nephandi showing up now. Did something create a whole lot more, or did something reveal them?<br /> <br /> Lots of ways this could have played out but the problems with Kaballah and Latin and such.<br /> <br /> Also, lots of ways this Great Work could have been done incorrectly, and perhapss that's the current problem. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25849-nybygehenna","name":"NYbyGehenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T10:19:45-07:00","id":1398817,"title":"","content":"Mage: the Awakening has 10 spheres. Entropy was broken up into Death for the destructive aspects and Fate for the aspects about destiny.<br /> <br /> Data is a Technocracy (and some Virtual Adepts) version of Correspondence. Dimensional Science is the Void Engineer version of Spirit. Primal Utility is the Syndicate version of Prime.<br /> <br /> Based on Phil Brucato's interview on Mage: the Podcast for M20 Book of the Fallen, there was less good information available early in the development of Mage than recently. Qlippothic, introduced in the Book of Madness, was much harder to find information on during that time than it is now--and if the discussion of Qlippothic ideas had not already appeared in Book of Madness, they may not have appeared in M20 Book of the Fallen.<br /> <br /> As for the Nephandi, at least from the preview manuscripts for M20 Technocracy Reloaded, the Technocracy has lost control of the world to a significant extent (your chronicle will vary). The bad parts of humanity have done a lot to make the world a more horrible place. Some of those are definitely Nephandi. Outside of game lore, I think if you see more Nephandi, it's the times we are living in plus the growth of the game and the writers to make the Nephandi less cartoony. There may not necessarily be more Nephandi in individual chronicles, but with a solid tome devoted to exploring them in many facets, it's easier to have them in the game.<br /> <br /> As for whether 10 spheres or 9 spheres, that's all pretty philosophical. If you're running 9, you're keeping to the core assumptions of Mage as even with Technocracy variant spheres, there are basically 9 spheres available to a character. If you run 10, then take a look at Mage: the Awakening and the Mage Translation Guide to figure out how Death and Fate were split up from Entropy. <br /> <br /> For other sphere combinations, well you're getting into the realm of game design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T05:43:56-07:00","id":1401469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398785-10th-sphere-and-what-those-new-spheres-mean?p=1398817#post1398817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage: the Awakening has 10 spheres. Entropy was broken up into Death for the destructive aspects and Fate for the aspects about destiny.<br /> <br /> Data is a Technocracy (and some Virtual Adepts) version of Correspondence. Dimensional Science is the Void Engineer version of Spirit. Primal Utility is the Syndicate version of Prime.<br /> <br /> Based on Phil Brucato's interview on Mage: the Podcast for M20 Book of the Fallen, there was less good information available early in the development of Mage than recently. Qlippothic, introduced in the Book of Madness, was much harder to find information on during that time than it is now--and if the discussion of Qlippothic ideas had not already appeared in Book of Madness, they may not have appeared in M20 Book of the Fallen.<br /> <br /> As for the Nephandi, at least from the preview manuscripts for M20 Technocracy Reloaded, the Technocracy has lost control of the world to a significant extent (your chronicle will vary). The bad parts of humanity have done a lot to make the world a more horrible place. Some of those are definitely Nephandi. Outside of game lore, I think if you see more Nephandi, it's the times we are living in plus the growth of the game and the writers to make the Nephandi less cartoony. There may not necessarily be more Nephandi in individual chronicles, but with a solid tome devoted to exploring them in many facets, it's easier to have them in the game.<br /> <br /> As for whether 10 spheres or 9 spheres, that's all pretty philosophical. If you're running 9, you're keeping to the core assumptions of Mage as even with Technocracy variant spheres, there are basically 9 spheres available to a character. If you run 10, then take a look at Mage: the Awakening and the Mage Translation Guide to figure out how Death and Fate were split up from Entropy.<br /> <br /> For other sphere combinations, well you're getting into the realm of game design.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also pointing out that the Spheres are as much an in-game construct as an out-of-game one. It's arguable that by convincing everyone to go with ten spheres, the Order and Batini shaped their paradigms to focus on ten rather than on other divisions, but ultimately the Spheres themselves exist out of game mostly to facilitate publishing and easier character and spell development. We've seen multiple alternative systems, including minor spheres in Revised as an optional rule and pillar systems in Dark Ages. But, publishing that many different sets of optionswould take up even more space than Mage already does, and would make later development of mechanics tricky (consider M20's &quot;How Do you DO That?&quot; and then imagine it trying to apture the various effects not with a universal system of spheres but with four pillars per featured tradition/convention/etc). <br /> <br /> Awakening uses ten Arcana but makes them relatively objective in nature - those ten concepts effectively govern every iteration of magic capable to a mage and every aspect of the world a mage can affect, but also exist in the arrangement they do because those ten arcana are the ones that supposedly exist in the Supernal Realms as some sort of platonic ideal that can be latched on to by a mage. Ascension lacks even the pretense in-universe of an objective world where the ideal versions of everything are (unless that's your paradigm), so the number and nature of the spheres depends in game on character perspective and out-of-game on the design work put in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}